# What has left the manifest and needs nothing done about it.
#
# One entry a line, said the way `console_migrations::holds` says it -- a path
# for a file, `enabled UNIT` or `masked UNIT` for a unit -- with the reason
# beside it. A name in here is somebody's decision and can be argued with. A
# name that is simply never mentioned is nothing at all, which is what this file
# exists to stop.
#
# Reaching for this file is the wrong move most of the time. The question to ask
# first is whether a machine that applied the commit before the removal is still
# holding the thing, and if it is, it wants a migration and not a line here.

# --- The rename, swept once by tools/console-migrate on 2026-08-29 -------------
#
# docs/rename.md section 3 is the whole of it, and step 6 is the sweep: every
# `legion-*` name the manifest had installed was moved to
# /var/tmp/console-migration-20260829-234115, which is still on the device. That
# attic is the evidence, and the device has been read since: no legion-named
# binary, unit, udev rule, sudoers file or profile survives on it. A migration
# repeating that work would find nothing to move on the one machine that ever
# had them, and a machine set up after the rename never had them at all.

